        "title": "Philosophy of Religion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Philosophy of religion is the application of philosophical method to religious claims —\ntreating them as propositions to be assessed, arguments to be evaluated, concepts to be\nclarified. It sits at the intersection of metaphysics, epistemology, ethics, and logic.\nThe central questions: Does God exist? If so, what is God like? Is religious experience\nevidence of anything? How should we reason about God given limited evidence?"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-PHILOSOPHY-RELIGION.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-PHILOSOPHY-RELIGION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:religious-studies:05-philosophy-religion, git-history:religious-studies:05-philosophy-religion]",
        "canonical_path": "religious-studies/05-PHILOSOPHY-RELIGION.md",
        "concepts": "[philosophy, religion]",
