        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Philosophy of Religion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              PHILOSOPHY OF RELIGION — PROBLEM MAP                   |\n|                                                                     |\n|  GOD'S EXISTENCE         GOD'S NATURE           RELIGIOUS BELIEF    |\n|  ---------------         -----------            ----------------    |\n|  Cosmological arg:       Omnipotence:           Evidentialism:      |\n|  First cause / KCA       paradoxes, coherence   evidence required   |\n|                                                                     |\n|  Ontological arg:        Omniscience:           Proper basicality:  |\n|  Greatest conceivable    foreknowledge vs.      belief can be       |\n|  being                   free will              basic (Plantinga)   |\n|                                                                     |\n|  Teleological arg:       Omnibenevolence:       Fideism:            |\n|  Design inference;       Problem of evil,       faith beyond/       |\n|  fine-tuning             theodicy               against reason      |\n|                                                                     |\n|  Ontological dis-        Immutability:          Wittgensteinian:    |\n|  mdloom: atheological     eternal vs.            religion as form    |\n|  arguments (evil,        everlasting            of life             |\n|  hiddenness)                                                        |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
