        "section": "religious-studies",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Philosophy of Religion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Leibniz's Principle of Sufficient Reason Version**:\nFor every fact, there must be a sufficient reason why it is so rather than otherwise.\nThe fact of the universe's existence requires a reason outside itself.\nOnly a necessary being (one whose essence includes existence — cannot NOT exist)\nprovides sufficient reason. That necessary being is God."
    }
